s10-3-p9 : Block
s10-3-p9 = prose (cons "A real protocol must also define message identities, duplication resistance, receipt acknowledgment, failure, reallocation, and the conditions under which credit can be returned. If messages may be duplicated without an idempotency rule, the conservation theorem fails: one in-flight allocation can be delivered twice. The required distinction is between *the stated invariant* and *the actual protocol transition rules*, not between mathematics and networking." nil)
